### 11. High-Level PR UI/UX Professionalize (Theme Inversion Fix)
- **Problem**: NativeWind v4 variables failed to cascade correctly during theme toggling, causing "eye-straining white text on white backgrounds" and inverted light/dark components.
- **Solution**: Refactored core primitives to use explicit `style={{ color: colors.X, backgroundColor: colors.Y }}` from `useTheme()`.
- **Affected Components**:
  - `Button.tsx` (fully refactored all variants to use `bgStyle` and `textStyle` objects)
  - `Card.tsx` (`CardTitle` text color explicitly set to `colors.foreground`)
  - `Input.tsx` (Label and error text explicitly set to `mutedForeground` and `destructive`)
  - `ScreenWrapper.tsx` (`PageHeader` and `SectionTitle` text colors explicitly mapped)

## Identified Known Issues (future work)
- Staff creation requires user UUID — poor UX; consider email-lookup endpoint
- `ChangePasswordModal` uses `presentationStyle="pageSheet"` which may clip Toast on iOS in some cases
- Passkey flow in MemberLoginScreen is simulated (no real WebAuthn on mobile RN)
- PublicHomeScreen plans: no client-side cache, re-fetches on every mount
